---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "31 May 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="GraceSoft PaperStack Privacy Policy — how we collect, use, and protect your information."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="legal-hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-05-31">{updated}</time>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose legal-prose">
        <p>
          GraceSoft ("we", "our", "us") operates the GraceSoft PaperStack
          website and design system. This Privacy Policy explains how we
          collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit
          our website or use our products. Please read this policy carefully. If
          you disagree with its terms, please discontinue use of the site.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Information You Provide</h3>
        <p>
          We may collect personal information you voluntarily provide when you:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fill out our contact or early-access form</li>
          <li>Subscribe to product updates or our newsletter</li>
          <li>Contact us directly by email or other means</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This may include your name, email address, company name, and any
          message content you submit.
        </p>

        <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
        <p>
          When you visit our website, we may automatically collect certain
          technical data including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Operating system</li>
          <li>Referring URLs</li>
          <li>Pages visited and time spent on pages</li>
          <li>IP address (anonymised where possible)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We use privacy-respecting analytics tools that do not set tracking
          cookies without consent.
        </p>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to enquiries and contact form submissions</li>
          <li>
            Send product updates, release notes, and announcements (with your
            consent)
          </li>
          <li>Improve the website and our products</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
          <li>Detect and prevent fraud or abuse</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We will never sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third
          parties.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA) or United
          Kingdom, our legal bases for processing personal data are:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent</strong> — for newsletter subscriptions and optional data
            collection
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — for improving our products and
            communicating with potential users
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal obligation</strong> — where required by applicable law
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Data Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
        <p>
          We may share your data with trusted third-party service providers who
          assist us in operating our website and delivering our service,
          including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email delivery services (e.g., for transactional emails)</li>
          <li>Analytics providers (with data minimisation in place)</li>
          <li>Form hosting services (e.g., Tally, Typeform)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All processors are bound by data processing agreements and are
          prohibited from using your data for their own purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may also disclose your information where required by law, court
          order, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of GraceSoft, our
          users, or the public.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Our website may use cookies for essential functionality and, with your
          consent, for analytics. You can control cookies through your browser
          settings. Disabling cookies may affect some features of the site.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes
          outlined in this policy or as required by law. Contact form data is
          retained for up to 2 years unless you request earlier deletion.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
          <li>Restrict or object to certain processing</li>
          <li>Data portability</li>
          <li>
            Withdraw consent at any time (without affecting prior lawful
            processing)
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@gracesoft.dev">privacy@gracesoft.dev</a>. We
          will respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to
          protect your personal data against accidental loss, unauthorised
          access, alteration, and disclosure. However, no method of transmission
          over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
          security.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our website and products are not directed at children under the age of
          13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If
          you believe we have inadvertently collected such information, please
          contact us and we will promptly delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Links to Third-Party Sites</h2>
        <p>
          Our website may contain links to external sites. We are not
          responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites and
          encourage you to review their privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify
          you of significant changes by updating the date at the top of this
          page. Your continued use of the website after changes constitutes
          acceptance of the revised policy.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions, concerns, or requests relating to this
          Privacy Policy, please contact:
        </p>
        <address>
          <strong>GraceSoft</strong><br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@gracesoft.dev">privacy@gracesoft.dev</a
          >
        </address>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-10);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-10);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--clr-black);
  }

  .legal-hero .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-3);
  }

  .legal-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(var(--fs-4xl), 6vw, var(--fs-6xl));
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--ff-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--clr-subtle);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  address {
    font-style: normal;
    background: var(--clr-indigo);
    border: 1px solid var(--clr-border);
    padding: var(--sp-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    line-height: 2;
  }
</style>
